-We connect these questions in a single study. First, we compare pointwise and paired supervision under a common neural architecture, then examine whether mode choice and departure timing benefit from separate model components. Second, we compare the fitted models with existing stated choices from Singapore and Shanghai, and query the Teacher on a subset of the same tasks to locate response differences. Third, we follow predictions through assignment, routing and event-observed journeys in MATSim. Figure~\ref{fig:workflow} summarizes the framework.
