 \section{Related work}
 \label{sec:related}
 \subsection{Language models as traveler agents}
-LLMs have been embedded directly into traveler-agent architectures. Recent work on GATSim and generative-agent cognitive modeling applies these architectures to urban mobility simulation \citep{gatsim2026,genagents2026}. Retrieval-augmented generation supplies relevant trip examples for mode-choice prediction \citep{ragbenchmark2026}, while LLM-augmented class-incremental learning addresses an evolving prediction task \citep{incremental2026}. These approaches place the language model within the prediction or agent system. Our study instead uses its outputs as offline supervision for a small numerical component.
