 The behavioral content of these outputs also requires evaluation. Research on the value of travel time examines the economic implications of LLM choices \citep{valuingtime2026}, and dual-agent modeling addresses alignment with human learning and adjustment \citep{dualagent2026}. This motivates separating fidelity to the source model from agreement with people. We compare changes in stated choices with changes in both Teacher and Student probabilities.
 
 \subsection{Choice models and modular prediction}
 Random-utility models relate mode probabilities to traveler characteristics and alternative attributes \citep{mcfadden1974conditional,ben1985discrete}. Generalized and mixed logit formulations provide richer representations of heterogeneity and dependence \citep{walker2002generalized,hensher2003mixed,train2009discrete}. Neural representations can also complement a specified utility function \citep{sifringer2020enhancing}. A compact model trained on LLM targets can therefore use either structured linear utilities or a shared neural representation.
 
